  {
   "id": 12,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "About this dashboard",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 38,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 6
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "### CI/CD Pipelines \u2014 how this works\n\n**Every GitHub Actions pipeline in the org, discovered dynamically.** The host collector\n(`grafana/cicd-collector/`, launchd `com.tommy.cicd-collector`, 5 min) lists every non-archived repo in\n**robogeosociety**, then writes to the `cicd` InfluxDB bucket:\n\n- `workflow_run` \u2014 one point per completed run (conclusion, duration, queue delay, attempt), timestamped at completion;\n- `workflow_inventory` \u2014 one point per workflow file per poll (the catalog panel, run-or-not);\n- `collector_poll` \u2014 a heartbeat with API-call and rate-limit accounting.\n\nA new repo or workflow file appears here within one poll \u2014 the **Repo/Workflow variables and every panel are\ndata-driven**, nothing on this dashboard names a pipeline. The workflow column in the tables links to the run in\nGitHub. Runs are sparse events: pick a range that covers pushes (default 7d), and expect gaps \u2014 the state timeline\nholds each pipeline's last conclusion until the next run.\n"
   }
  }
